# External website webview Feature Overview

This page contains 2 major parts, preferably achieved with 2 webviews:
- A narbar that aligns to the main app's theme. It contains a back button (goes back to the feed) and a menu dropdown. The dropdown list has translation toggle and read aloud features. More features are to be added in the future.
- A main webview (not iframe) that opens an external URL. 

## Navbar
This should be part of the main app, meaning it manages the current page, states and route. 
The menu button shows a dropdown as overlay over other parts of the page (so it overflows the navbar). We have a open mind of how to display this due to technology limitations, for example: when it's hard to overflow outside of navbar's webview, we could consider showing a full screen overlay with modal, or a drawer pops from the bottom of the screen. Given this page shows multiple webviews, the dropdown or overlay needs to show on top of everything.

## External website webview
This is a separate webview inside of this page. It could be dettached from the main app flow, meaning a separate Tauri webview in the window. 
- It shows uncontrolled contents from arbitrary external websites. 
- It filters network traffic from the displayed website, and potentially blocks ads. 
- It can extract all HTML content from the website, then inject modified contents back, like a browser plugin. 
- It does above features via a common interface to the webview across different system platforms. For example it should work the same way in both Android and iOS. 
- All above features are controlled via the main app. For example, selecting "toggle translation" from the nav bar will extract the HTML content and trigger a tranlation command to the Tauri backend, then inject response back into this webview. 

